# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Dong-Jin Kim et al. (2025). A Universal Augmentation Framework for Long-Range Electrostatics in Machine Learning Interatomic Potentials.
#   Journal of Chemical Theory and Computation. doi:10.1021/acs.jctc.5c01400  arXiv:2507.14302v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2507.14302v1 (sha256 d63fef9763c6aac9...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 226 (Software/implementation). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/kim2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the LES library and its combination with MACE
# (MACE-LES; MACELES-OFF), trained on SPICE, with its test MAEs and RMSEs
# on the seven SPICE-derived test subsets (Table III). The baseline and
# LES-augmented MACE, NequIP, CACE and CHGNet models for bulk water,
# dipeptides and Au2 on MgO(001) have errors only in figures (Figs. 2-4)
# and are not encoded; the MACE-OFF23 values of Table III are taken from
# the MACE-OFF paper.

