# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - LES (introduced in cheng2025 with CACE) is released here as a library and combined with MACE as MACELES-OFF; recorded as the new registry method MACE-LES derived from MACE, stated in the Abstract ('compatible with any short-range MLIP ... integration with methods such as MACE'). The LES-augmented NequIP and CHGNet models are not given registry methods because they have no tabulated errors.
# - Table III's caption says RMSE but it contains MAE and RMSE blocks; both are encoded. 13 outlier PubChem configurations were removed from the 34,093 test structures as in MACE-OFF.
# - The Au2-MgO(001) wetting energy differences (Table I) are not accuracy metrics of the schema. The level of theory of SPICE is not restated (BEC references at wB97M-D3(BJ)/def2-SVP in PySCF).
# - No training or inference timing is given.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
